    <briefdescription>
<para>A begin/end timestamp pair used to measure elapsed time. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamps" kindref="compound">timestamps</ref></computeroutput> stores an optional begin <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamp" kindref="compound">timestamp</ref></computeroutput> and an optional end <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamp" kindref="compound">timestamp</ref></computeroutput>. When both are available, <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamps_1a7e7ade6bb02af23d65e5ceaa958052dd" kindref="member">compute_elapsed_time()</ref></computeroutput> derives the elapsed interval in milliseconds and microseconds.</para>
<para>Typical usage in the framework:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Call <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamps_1a1b2077718469ade9fda2e257a0d06293" kindref="member">timestamp_begin()</ref></computeroutput> just before the test suite or session body executes.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Call <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamps_1aeb4873587b5be066c69c0ef26d64640b" kindref="member">timestamp_end()</ref></computeroutput> immediately after it completes.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Pass the elapsed values to the reporter.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>If the platform does not provide a monotonic clock, the <computeroutput>std::optional</computeroutput> members remain empty and <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamps_1a125c87d852257c18749074be3b698ed1" kindref="member">has_timestamps()</ref></computeroutput> returns <computeroutput>false</computeroutput>, so that the reporter can skip timing output.</para>
<para>The class is non-copyable and non-movable to prevent accidental sharing of live timing state. </para>
